title: v1 COMPLETE — atelier studio ships locally launchable, LLM↔human loop live, pack v0.1.0 in
summary: 'Final v1 close. 15/15 tasks shipped, 12 commits, 649/651 tests passing (+71 new since session start), 24 university entries across 4 tracks. atelier studio is now a real local-first product: npm install → atelier studio → land in scaffolded welcome.atelier → drop a photo (replaces placeholder background) → add overlays via layer-type picker or recipe → watch an external MCP client (Claude Desktop / atelier-mcp via the new WebSocket transport) mutate the doc live with attribution toast and Cmd-Z undo → export to PNG via atelier export-image. The symbiotic loop the cold review asked for is real and end-to-end: DocumentStore.onChange + AtelierStudio.applyMutation + WS bridge at /bridge + MCP-over-WS transport at /mcp + suppress-notify flag + last-write-wins conflict policy + source-tagged ops (human|llm|system). Localhost-only security (^localhost-only gate, 127.0.0.1 bind, Origin check) covers HTTP and WS upgrade. Recipe overlay_rules promoted to Phase 1.5 with handle + page-number applyRecipeToOverlay translator. Pack v0.1.0 ships ATEL-001 (Hello), 101 (Document Model), 201 (MCP Authoring), 301 (Visual System) — 24 validated entries, paradigm university validate green. Multi-agent orchestration pattern proved out: 6 paradigm:builder agents across 4 rounds in background, me on pack authoring + integration in foreground, advisor + paradigm:architect + paradigm:reviewer + general-purpose dx consult to set the v1 cut list. Two skipped tests pending node-canvas binary; one carousel-batch driver remains for v1.1.'
